course: dictionary
lesson: 1055
title: Botanic and the world of plants
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Botanic is an adjective, a word that describes a noun. It means to do with plants and the study of plants. Botanical means the same thing. A botanic garden is a garden where many kinds of plants are grown for study and for people to see.
explain: Use context to work out a new word. «The titan arum blooms only once every few years, and when one blooms in a botanic garden crowds queue to see and smell it.» The crowds queuing to see a plant tell you that a botanic garden is a place where people go to look at plants. Botanic must be about plants.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. Try «a garden of plants» in place of «a botanic garden». Does it still make sense? It does, so you have understood the word. Botany is the study of plants, and a botanist is a person who studies plants.
fact: Botanic means to do with plants and the study of plants.
fact: Botany is the study of plants, and a botanist is a person who studies plants.
fact: «A botanic garden» is a garden where many kinds of plants are grown for study and for people to see.
fact: Kew Gardens in London is a famous botanic garden.
fact: «The titan arum blooms only once every few years» shows that some plants are rare and special.
exercise: What does botanic mean? | To do with stars and planets | *To do with plants and the study of plants | To do with the sea | To do with old buildings
exercise: «A botanic garden» is a place where many kinds of plants are grown for study and for people to see. Which of these is the best example? | *A garden with many kinds of plants that visitors can look at | A shop that sells shoes | A swimming pool with a diving board | A school for learning to sail
exercise: What is a botanist? | A person who builds houses | A person who sails ships | A person who writes plays | *A person who studies plants
test: Kew Gardens in London is a famous botanic garden. What is it mainly for? | Teaching children to swim | Keeping ships safe in the harbour | Selling cars to visitors | *Growing many kinds of plants for study and for people to see
test: Which word means to do with plants? | Gigantic | Galactic | *Botanical | Robotic
exam: Maya says botanic means to do with animals. Is she right? | *No, botanic means to do with plants and the study of plants | Yes, botanic means to do with animals | No, botanic means to do with machines | Yes, botanic means to do with the sky
